onal range which was achieved by its structural lightness and an almost total lack of protection for the crew, which was its weakness when confronted with American fighters. A total of 2,435 G4Ms were built, including a few variants.","LocalizedString":"The Mitsubishi G4M, nicknamed Betty by the Allies, was the main twin-engine, land-based bomber used by the Imperial Japanese Navy Air Service during WWII. The G4Ms were first used in service in 1940 and were mostly used as torpedo bombers in anti-shipping roles. The aircraft performed very well, especially in operational range which was achieved by its structural lightness and an almost total lack of protection for the crew, which was its weakness when confronted with American fighters. A total of 2,435 G4Ms were built, including a few variants."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Basic","isReserved":true,"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Deployment"],"hasDeployment":true,"soundBlowUp":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Explosion_Medium'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Misc/Explosion_Medium.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Japan/t_betty_2.t_betty_2","SubPathString":""},"ImageAnchor":"EImageAnchor::Bot","artist":"Japanese WWII postcard","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/G4M1_BETTY.G4M1_BETTY","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":187.0},"historyPhotoSource":"http://www.ijnafpics.com/jbwg4m1.htm","historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_g4m1_betty_photo","SourceString":"Mitsubishi G4M1, ca 1940.","LocalizedString":"Mitsubishi G4M1, ca 1940."},"historyTypeDescription":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_unit_g4m1_betty_header","SourceString":"Medium Bomber","LocalizedString":"Medium Bomber"},"blowUpExplosion":{"ObjectName":"ParticleSystem'P_ExplosionAircraftM'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Effects/Explosions/Medium/Aircraft/P_ExplosionAircraftM.193"},"blowUpCam